/* ============================================================
   src/pages/architects.astro  →  wrightcm.co/architects
   The WCM Architect Alliance: design partner landing page.

   DROP-IN NOTES
   1. Save this file as  src/pages/architects.astro
   2. Uses Base.astro, so it inherits Header, Footer, global.css,
      the Inter webfont, and the RB2B script automatically.
   3. Page-specific CSS is scoped under .aap in the <style is:global>
      block at the bottom, same pattern as brokers.astro. It reuses
      global.css tokens (--navy, --red, --line, --bg-soft…) so colors
      and fonts stay centrally managed. Nothing is hardcoded.
   4. To add "Architects" to the main nav, add this <li> to
      src/components/Header.astro inside <ul class="nav-links">:

         <li><a href="/architects">Architects</a></li>

      (suggested position: next to /brokers)
   5. The enrollment form posts to Formspree at
      https://formspree.io/f/xqeojvde, the same endpoint /brokers and
      /contact already use, so submissions land in the existing inbox
      and notify jwright@wrightcm.co. Submission is AJAX: the architect
      stays on the page and the form is replaced by a confirmation.
      Every field carries a human-readable name= attribute, which is
      what Formspree prints as the label in the notification email.
      _subject is rewritten on submit to carry the firm name, and
      name="email" sets the reply-to so replying goes to the architect.
   6. There is no compensation content anywhere in this page and there
      must not be. WCM pays architects nothing under this program. The
      only paid item is the Capacity Walk, whose fee is never published
      here: it is quoted per engagement.
   ============================================================ */
