    <div class="aap-grid3" style="margin-top:36px">
      <div class="aap-card"><div class="aap-num">01</div><h3>The Trade Sheet and the Market Note</h3><p>Two standing one-pagers for your building type, refreshed every quarter and built from our own completed projects rather than a national index. <strong>The Trade Sheet</strong> is current unit costs and swap values: what a dock position costs, what a foot of clear height costs, the delta between two envelope assemblies, what a floor drain costs installed, what sanitary wall and ceiling finishes run per square foot. <strong>The Market Note</strong> is what we are seeing in the trade market right now: which packages are drawing bidders and which are coming back thin, where labor is tight, what is escalating. Take them into an Owner meeting and answer in the room.</p></div>
      <div class="aap-card"><div class="aap-num">02</div><h3>The Number Check, 3 business days</h3><p>Send us the program, the square footage and the Owner's budget before you commit your firm to it. You get back a private read on whether that number is real for this building type in this market, and if it is not, what it would have to be. We have priced this work at every scale from a 20,000 SF conversion to a 700,000 SF greenfield plant, so most of the time this is recall as much as calculation.</p></div>
      <div class="aap-card"><div class="aap-num">03</div><h3>Rapid Range, 2 business days</h3><p>Building type, square footage and program in. A parametric cost range out, stated at plus or minus 25%, with the basis printed on it. No drawings required and none wanted: this is the number for the conversation you are having this week, not the one you will eventually bid. Ask for it as often as it is useful.</p></div>
      <div class="aap-card"><div class="aap-num">04</div><h3>Design Option Pricing, 5 business days</h3><p>You are weighing two or three ways to do something. Send them over and we price each one, with the basis and the assumptions written down. Want our read on what the market is doing to any of them, ask and you will get it. It comes back to you, and what happens to it next is your call.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ THE WALK ============ -->
<section id="walk">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">The next step</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">Existing Conditions and Capacity Walk.</h2>
