    <div class="aap-tablewrap">
      <table class="aap-tbl">
        <tr><th style="width:24%"></th><th>What it says</th></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Your option, in your words</strong></td><td>Restated exactly as you sent it, so you can see we priced the thing you actually asked about.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>The number</strong></td><td>A cost for that option and its delta against the others, with the basis and the unit rates it was built from.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>What moves with it</strong></td><td>Schedule effect, procurement consequences, and any bid coverage risk that comes attached to the choice.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>What we assumed</strong></td><td>Every assumption, listed, so you can correct one and ask again free.</td></tr>
        <tr class="hot"><td><strong>Our read, if you asked for it</strong></td><td>What we are seeing in the market on each approach. Left out entirely if you did not ask.</td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="aap-card aap-navy" style="margin-top:24px">
      <h3 style="color:#fff">Why a structural engineer is the one reading it</h3>
      <p style="margin-top:10px;max-width:88ch">What blows a budget on this building type is never finishes. It is the slab that will not take the equipment load as drawn, the roof framing that will not carry the equipment above it, the service that has to be upsized before anything else can be sized, and the column line sitting exactly where the production line has to run. <strong style="color:#fff">Those move the number by six figures in a single decision, so those are the questions worth asking us first.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ PROTECTION ============ -->
<section class="section-soft" id="protect">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">What we put in writing</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">Your client stays your client. Your design stays yours.</h2>
    <div class="aap-2col" style="margin-top:30px">
      <div class="aap-card aap-tint"><h3>Non-circumvention, both directions</h3><p>On a project you bring us we will not propose another architect to that Owner, will not offer to carry the design ourselves, and will not pursue that Owner's other projects without looping you in. If they contact us directly, we tell you within one business day.</p></div>
      <div class="aap-card aap-tint"><h3>Nothing reaches your Owner without you</h3><p>Every deliverable is addressed to you. We do not copy your Owner, we do not send cost opinions behind you, and we do not communicate a view on the design to your client without you in the room. What you do with any of it is entirely your call.</p></div>
      <div class="aap-card aap-tint"><h3>We do not perform or direct design</h3><p>We provide cost, constructability and market input. We do not issue drawings, do not direct design, and do not assume responsibility for your instruments of service. You remain the design professional of record, and nothing we provide substitutes for design, engineering or code review by a licensed professional.</p></div>
      <div class="aap-card aap-tint"><h3>Your drawings stay yours, and stay private</h3><p>Anything you send us is used solely to produce what you asked for, is never shown to a landlord, seller or third party without your consent, and is returned or destroyed on request. We will sign your Owner's NDA or ours, whichever you prefer.</p></div>
    </div>

    <div class="aap-card aap-navy" style="margin-top:22px">
      <span class="eyebrow" style="color:#ff8c87">The Design Partner Panel</span>
      <h3 style="color:#fff;margin-top:10px">We send work back.</h3>
      <p style="margin-top:10px;max-width:92ch">Every design-build project we deliver needs an architect, and we would rather hand that to a firm that already knows how we build than run a selection. <strong style="color:#fff">Panel firms hear about a pursuit in their building types before we have committed to a design team</strong>, along with the Owner requirements we pick up from processors, cold storage operators and senior living developers who need more building than they have.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:10px;max-width:92ch"><strong style="color:#fff">How you get on it: one Capacity Walk, or one design-build project delivered together.</strong> That is the whole requirement. No submission, no SOQ, no interview. The point is that we have actually worked together once before we put your name in front of an Owner.</p>
      <div class="aap-panel3">
      <div><strong>What we send you</strong><p>The pursuit, the Owner, the program and the schedule, before we have committed to a design team. Pass on any of it with no effect on your standing.</p></div>
      <div><strong>What it is worth</strong><p>A negotiated design commission you did not compete for, on a project where the Contractor already understands what the drawings are going to cost.</p></div>
      <div><strong>What it is not</strong><p>Exclusivity in either direction, or a promise of volume. It is a standing shortlist and a phone call that arrives before the RFP does.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ HOW IT WORKS ============ -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
