<!-- ============ FAQ ============ -->
<section class="section-soft" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap aap-narrow">
    <span class="eyebrow">The questions architects actually ask</span>
    <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-bottom:30px">Straight answers.</h2>
    <details open><summary>Why would you give this away?</summary><p>Because we would rather be in the conversation while a building is still being decided than show up with four other bidders at the end. And on design-build we are the ones hiring the architect, so this is how we find the firms we want on our teams. We have managed $820M of this work. A large share of what we look at never gets built, and plenty of the rest goes to somebody else. We are set up for that.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can you really price my project in two days?</summary><p>We can give you a defensible range in two days. We cannot give you an estimate, and neither can anybody else. The Rapid Range is parametric off building type, square footage and program, it is stated at plus or minus 25%, and it says so on the page. That is the number for the conversation you are having this week. The number you bid comes out of real preconstruction, and that is a different exercise with a different timeline.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is this just free value engineering? I do not want my design second-guessed.</summary><p>It is the opposite, and the difference is who starts it. We do not review your set and come back with findings. You send us the approaches you are weighing and we price those. If you want our read on any of them you will get it, and if you do not ask, you will not hear it. What we say about your design unprompted is nothing.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What does my Owner see?</summary><p>Whatever you decide to show them. Every deliverable is addressed to you. We do not copy your client, and we do not put a cost opinion in front of them behind your back. That is a term of the program rather than a courtesy.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How do I get on the Design Partner Panel?</summary><p>One Capacity Walk, or one design-build project delivered together. Nothing else. There is no submission and no interview, because the walk already told us what we needed to know about working with you. Once you are on it, you hear about design-build pursuits in your building types before we have committed to a design team.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Are you going to take the design in-house?</summary><p>We have no design studio and no intention of building one. On every design-build project we deliver we hire an architect, which is the reason this program exists. On a project you bring us, we will not propose another architect to that Owner and we will not offer to carry the design ourselves.</p></details>
    <details><summary>I already have CMs I call for budget numbers.</summary><p>Keep them. Use us for the questions a general contractor guesses at: refrigeration and process loads, sanitary construction, USDA-driven detailing, service capacity, and building around production that cannot stop. It is all we build, and we have done it at 700,000 SF.</p></details>
    <details><summary>My client selects their own contractor, and it goes to bid.</summary><p>So do some of ours. Run the selection. By the time it happens you will have seen how we think about cost, how fast we move and whether our numbers hold, which is a better basis for a decision than a proposal and an interview.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What if the project never gets built?</summary><p>Then you got real cost intelligence during design and we got a look at how your firm works. That is a normal outcome here, not a disappointing one.</p></details>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ ENROLL ============ -->
<section class="aap-final" id="enroll">
  <div class="wrap aap-ctagrid">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow" style="color:#ff8c87">Start here</span>
      <h2>Start with the sheet. Then give us something harder.</h2>
      <p>Send your building types and the current Trade Sheet and Market Note come back the same week. After that, the fastest way to find out whether any of this is worth your time is to hand us the project you are least sure about.</p>
      <ul class="aap-check">
        <li>Trade Sheet and Market Note: the week you ask</li>
        <li>Number Check: 3 business days</li>
        <li>Rapid Range: 2 business days, at plus or minus 25% with the basis stated</li>
        <li>Priced options: 5 business days</li>
        <li>A Design Partner Panel seat once we have walked a building together</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="aap-contact">
        <strong>Jeremy Wright</strong> &middot; Principal, Wright Construction Management<br>
        <strong>jwright@wrightcm.co</strong> &middot; <strong>(717) 422-7148</strong><br>
        1 E Erie St, Suite 525, Chicago, IL 60611<br>
        Chicagoland &middot; Northern Illinois &middot; Northwest Indiana &middot; Southern Wisconsin
      </div>
    </div>

    <form class="aap-form" id="aapForm" action="https://formspree.io/f/xqeojvde" method="POST">
      <input type="hidden" name="_subject" id="af_subject" value="New Architect Alliance request (wrightcm.co/architects)">
      <input type="hidden" name="form_type" value="Architect Alliance request">
      <input type="text" name="_gotcha" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;left:-9999px;width:1px;height:1px;opacity:0">
      <div class="row">
        <div><label for="af_name">Your name</label><input id="af_name" name="Architect name" required placeholder="Jane Architect, AIA"></div>
        <div><label for="af_firm">Firm</label><input id="af_firm" name="Firm" placeholder="Firm name"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <div><label for="af_email">Email</label><input id="af_email" name="email" type="email" required placeholder="you@firm.com"></div>
        <div><label for="af_phone">Mobile</label><input id="af_phone" name="Mobile" placeholder="(312) 555-0100"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <div><label for="af_types">Your building types</label><input id="af_types" name="Building types" placeholder="Cold storage, food processing, senior living"></div>
        <div><label for="af_owner">Owner / end user</label><input id="af_owner" name="Owner / end user" placeholder="So we can register it to you"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <div><label for="af_sf">Approx. SF</label><input id="af_sf" name="Approx. SF" placeholder="90,000"></div>
        <div><label for="af_phase">Design phase</label><input id="af_phase" name="Design phase" placeholder="SD / DD / CD"></div>
      </div>
      <label for="af_use">What do you want, and what should we know?</label>
      <textarea id="af_use" name="What they want / notes" placeholder="Just the Trade Sheet is a perfectly good answer. Otherwise: the process and temperature, USDA or not, the Owner's budget if there is one, target occupancy, and the options you want priced."></textarea>
      <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Send It Over</button>
      <p class="aap-formnote">Everything we produce is addressed to you, not to your client.</p>
    </form>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap aap-legal">
    This page summarizes the WCM Architect Alliance and is not a contract; participation is governed by the Design Partner Terms. All services described are provided at no charge except the Existing Conditions and Capacity Walk, which carries a flat fee quoted in writing before the visit and credited in full against WCM's fee if the Owner engages WCM for the project within twelve months of the walk. Preconstruction deliverables are preliminary, order-of-magnitude and advisory, state the confidence band and assumptions under which they were produced, are not a bid, a guaranteed price or a certification, and do not substitute for design, engineering, cost estimating or code review by a licensed professional. A Rapid Range is a parametric range and is not an estimate. Deliverables are provided to the Partner and not to any Owner. Design Partner Panel participation confers eligibility for consideration on design-build pursuits and is not a guarantee of engagement or of any volume of work. Turnaround targets run on business days and depend on WCM receiving the required information and access. Performance figures reflect the historic project portfolio of WCM leadership.
  </div>
</section>
`;
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="aap" set:html={bodyHtml}></div>

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var form = document.getElementById('aapForm');
      if (!form) return;
      form.addEventListener('submit', function (e) {
        e.preventDefault();
        var g = function (id) { var el = document.getElementById(id); return el ? (el.value || '').trim() : ''; };
        // Subject line carries the firm so the inbox is scannable without opening.
        var subj = document.getElementById('af_subject');
        if (subj) subj.value = 'Architect Alliance: ' + (g('af_firm') || g('af_name') || 'new request');
        var btn = form.querySelector('button[type="submit"]');
        var label = btn ? btn.textContent : '';
        if (btn) { btn.disabled = true; btn.textContent = 'Sending...'; }
        var reset = function () { if (btn) { btn.disabled = false; btn.textContent = label; } };
        fetch(form.action, {
          method: 'POST',
          body: new FormData(form),
          headers: { 'Accept': 'application/json' }
        }).then(function (r) {
          if (r.ok) {
            form.innerHTML =
              '<div class="aap-thanks">'
              + '<h3>Got it. Thank you.</h3>'
              + '<p>Jeremy Wright has your request and will reply personally. Here is what happens next:</p>'
              + '<ol>'
              + '<li>The current Trade Sheet and Market Note for your building types come back this week.</li>'
              + '<li>Anything you asked us to price runs on the posted turnaround, with the basis and the band stated on it.</li>'
              + '<li>Everything is addressed to you. Nothing goes to your client unless you send it.</li>'
              + '</ol>'
              + '<p class="aap-thanks-contact">Sooner than that? Email <a href="mailto:jwright@wrightcm.co">jwright@wrightcm.co</a> or call (717) 422-7148.</p>'
              + '</div>';
          } else {
            r.json().then(function (d) {
              reset();
              var msg = (d && d.errors && d.errors.map(function (x) { return x.message; }).join(', ')) || '';
              alert(msg || 'Something went wrong. Please email jwright@wrightcm.co and we will pick it up from there.');
            }).catch(function () {
              reset();
              alert('Something went wrong. Please email jwright@wrightcm.co and we will pick it up from there.');
            });
          }
        }).catch(function () {
          reset();
          alert('Network error. Please email jwright@wrightcm.co and we will pick it up from there.');
        });
      });
    })();
  </script>

  <style is:global>
/* ============================================================
   Architect Alliance page, scoped under .aap
   Inherits every color, font and spacing token from global.css.
   No hardcoded brand values: change global.css, this follows.
   Mirrors brokers.astro so the two programs stay visually identical.
   ============================================================ */

/* global.css sets .hero-inner{padding:104px 0 96px}, which lands after
   .wrap{padding:0 24px} at equal specificity and zeroes the hero's side
   padding. Above 1200px the max-width hides it; on a phone the hero text
   sits flush against the screen edge. Restored here for this page only.
   The same thing happens on the homepage and /brokers; fixing it in
   global.css would correct all three at once. */
.aap .hero-inner{padding-left:24px;padding-right:24px}

.aap .aap-2col{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:22px;align-items:start}
.aap .aap-grid3{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px}
.aap .aap-narrow{max-width:900px}

.aap .aap-pull{border-left:4px solid var(--red);padding:6px 0 6px 22px;font-size:clamp(1.2rem,2.3vw,1.65rem);font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.3;letter-spacing:-.02em}

.aap .aap-card{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:26px;background:#fff}
.aap .aap-card.aap-tint{background:var(--bg-soft);border-color:#dbe5f0}
.aap .aap-card.aap-navy{background:var(--navy);border-color:var(--navy);color:#fff}
.aap .aap-card.aap-navy p{color:#cfe0f0}
.aap .aap-card h3{font-size:1.12rem;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--navy)}
.aap .aap-card p{color:var(--muted);font-size:.96rem}
.aap .aap-card p + p{margin-top:10px}
.aap .aap-num{width:30px;height:30px;border-radius:8px;background:var(--red);color:#fff;font-weight:900;font-size:.8rem;display:grid;place-items:center;margin-bottom:12px}
.aap .aap-h3{font-size:1.18rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:-.02em;margin-bottom:6px}
.aap .aap-sm{font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted)}
.aap .aap-fine{font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin-top:22px}
.aap .aap-kick{display:inline-block;font-size:.66rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--red);margin-bottom:8px}
.aap .aap-kick.aap-kick-m{color:var(--muted)}

/* design partner panel strip inside the navy card */
.aap .aap-panel3{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:16px;margin-top:20px;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18)}
.aap .aap-panel3 strong{color:#fff;font-size:.92rem;display:block;margin-bottom:4px}
.aap .aap-panel3 p{color:#9db6cf;font-size:.85rem;margin:0}

/* tables */
.aap .aap-tablewrap{overflow-x:auto}
.aap .aap-tbl{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.95rem;margin-top:18px}
.aap .aap-tbl th{background:var(--navy);color:#fff;text-align:left;padding:13px 16px;font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:800}
.aap .aap-tbl td{padding:13px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);vertical-align:top;color:var(--ink)}
.aap .aap-tbl tr:nth-child(even) td{background:var(--bg-soft)}
.aap .aap-tbl td.n,.aap .aap-tbl th.n{text-align:right}
.aap .aap-tbl td.n{font-weight:800;color:var(--navy)}
.aap .aap-tbl tr.hot td{background:#fdf0ef}
.aap .aap-tbl tr.hot td.n{color:var(--red)}

/* callout rows */
.aap .aap-promise{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:18px;padding:17px 22px;border:1px solid #f3cdcb;background:#fdf6f5;border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;color:var(--ink)}
.aap .aap-promise strong{color:var(--navy)}
.aap .aap-promise .pen{flex:0 0 auto;font-weight:800;color:var(--red);font-size:.86rem;text-align:right}

/* steps */
.aap .aap-step{display:flex;gap:18px;margin-bottom:24px}
.aap .aap-step .n{flex:0 0 42px;height:42px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--navy);color:#fff;font-weight:900;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:1.05rem}
.aap .aap-step h3{font-size:1.06rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:3px}
.aap .aap-step p{color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem}

/* faq */
.aap details{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:10px;background:#fff;overflow:hidden}
.aap details summary{cursor:pointer;padding:16px 20px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:14px}
.aap details summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
.aap details summary:after{content:"+";font-size:1.4rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--red);line-height:1}
.aap details[open] summary:after{content:"\2013"}
.aap details p{padding:0 20px 18px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem}

/* final cta */
.aap .aap-final{background:#0b2138;position:relative;overflow:hidden;color:#fff}
.aap .aap-final:before{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;background:radial-gradient(900px 600px at 20% 0%,rgba(29,80,129,.85),transparent 62%)}
.aap .aap-final .wrap{position:relative;z-index:2}
.aap .aap-final h2{color:#fff;font-size:clamp(1.7rem,3.4vw,2.5rem);font-weight:900;letter-spacing:-.03em;margin-top:10px}
.aap .aap-final p{color:#cfe0f0;max-width:56ch;margin-top:14px}
.aap .aap-ctagrid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.05fr .95fr;gap:44px;align-items:start}
.aap .aap-check{list-style:none;margin-top:22px}
.aap .aap-check li{position:relative;padding-left:24px;margin-bottom:11px;font-size:.97rem;color:#cfe0f0}
.aap .aap-check li:before{content:"";position:absolute;left:0;top:.5em;width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:3px;background:#ff6b64}
.aap .aap-contact{margin-top:26px;font-size:.94rem;color:#cfe0f0;line-height:1.9}
.aap .aap-contact strong{color:#fff}

/* form */
.aap .aap-form{background:rgba(255,255,255,.06);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18);border-radius:16px;padding:26px}
.aap .aap-form label{display:block;font-size:.68rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.13em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#9db6cf;margin:0 0 6px}
.aap .aap-form input,.aap .aap-form textarea{width:100%;background:rgba(255,255,255,.09);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.2);border-radius:9px;padding:11px 13px;color:#fff;font-family:var(--font);font-size:.94rem;margin-bottom:15px;outline:none}
.aap .aap-form input::placeholder,.aap .aap-form textarea::placeholder{color:#7d99b6}
.aap .aap-form input:focus,.aap .aap-form textarea:focus{border-color:#ff8c87}
.aap .aap-form textarea{min-height:74px;resize:vertical}
.aap .aap-form .row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:14px}
.aap .aap-form .btn{width:100%;justify-content:center}
.aap .aap-formnote{font-size:.74rem;color:#9db6cf;margin-top:12px;line-height:1.5}
.aap .aap-thanks{padding:6px 2px}
.aap .aap-thanks h3{color:#fff;font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:12px;letter-spacing:-.01em}
.aap .aap-thanks p{color:#cfe0f0;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.6;margin-bottom:14px}
.aap .aap-thanks ol{margin:0 0 4px;padding-left:20px;color:#e6eef7;font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.6}
.aap .aap-thanks ol li{margin-bottom:9px}
.aap .aap-thanks .aap-thanks-contact{font-size:.85rem;color:#9db6cf;margin-top:18px;margin-bottom:0}
.aap .aap-thanks a{color:#ff8c87;font-weight:600}
.aap .aap-legal{margin-top:34px;font-size:.72rem;line-height:1.6;color:#6f8aa6;display:block;max-width:var(--maxw)}

@media(max-width:980px){
  .aap .aap-grid3{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}
  .aap .aap-panel3{grid-template-columns:1fr}
}
@media(max-width:880px){
  .aap .aap-2col,.aap .aap-grid3,.aap .aap-ctagrid{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  .aap .aap-ctagrid{gap:30px}
}
@media(max-width:640px){
  .aap .aap-promise{flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;gap:8px}
  .aap .aap-promise .pen{text-align:left}
  .aap .aap-form .row{grid-template-columns:1fr}
}
  </style>
</Base>
